            <article class="universal-content">
                <h2>Universal Analytics to Google Analytics 4 Migration</h2>
                <p>
                    As Google continues evolving its analytics offerings, businesses must stay ahead of the curve and ensure that their data collection and analysis processes remain up-to-date. Google Analytics 4 (GA4) is the latest generation of the platform, designed to collect event-based data from both websites and apps. It is set to replace Universal Analytics by July 2023 completely. Our Google Analytics 4 consultants can help you seamlessly transition from Universal Analytics to GA4, ensuring your organization is prepared for the future of web analytics. Here's how our Google Analytics 4 consulting services can help you with the migration.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>

        <div class="universal-info">
            <article class="info">
                <div class="header">
                    <img src="/assets/images/services/google-analytics-consultant/universal-1.svg" alt="Icon">
                    <h4>Audit and Assessment:</h4>
                </div>
                <p>
                    We'll start by conducting a thorough audit of your existing Universal Analytics setup, identifying any tracking issues, gaps in data collection, and opportunities for improvement. This assessment will help us understand your current analytics needs and ensure a smooth transition to Google Analytics 4.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="info">
                <div class="header">
                    <img src="/assets/images/services/google-analytics-consultant/universal-2.svg" alt="Icon">
                    <h4>Data Integration and Validation:</h4>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Once your GA4 setup is complete, we'll help you integrate your new Google Analytics 4 data with your existing Universal Analytics data, ensuring you maintain access to historical data and insights. We'll also validate your GA4 data to ensure accuracy and reliability.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="info">
                <div class="header">
                    <img src="/assets/images/services/google-analytics-consultant/universal-3.svg" alt="Icon">
                    <h4>Custom GA4 Configuration:</h4>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Our Google Analytics 4 consultants will work with you to develop a customized configuration that aligns with your organization's goals and requirements. This includes setting up event tracking, custom dimensions, measuring eCommerce, and other advanced features to ensure that your GA4 implementation captures the most valuable data for your business.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="info">
                <div class="header">
                    <img src="/assets/images/services/google-analytics-consultant/universal-4.svg" alt="Icon">
                    <h4>GA4 Training and Support:</h4>
                </div>
                <p>
                    With new metrics, and new ways of getting insight into website visitor data, Google Analytics 4 is significantly different than Universal Analytics. To ensure that your team is well-equipped to manage your new setup, we'll provide training on the <a href="https://alphaefficiency.com/google-analytics-4-benefits">Google Analytics 4 benefits</a>, features, and best practices.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
